course: dictionary
lesson: 10263
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A toolbox is a box for keeping and carrying tools such as a hammer, screwdrivers and a tape measure. You can picture one in a shed or in the boot of a car. That is the first meaning, and it is the one you will know best.
explain: Toolbox can also mean a set of skills, methods or ideas you can use for a job. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Animals find the way with a whole toolbox: the Sun by day, the stars by night, coastlines and rivers, smells.» There is no box here, so toolbox must mean a set of ways to find the way.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence to check it. «Writers have a toolbox of hooks: speech, action, a sound ("CRASH!")» Can you swap in a box of tools? No. Can you swap in a set of ways to catch a reader's attention? Yes, so that is the meaning.
fact: A toolbox is a box for keeping and carrying tools such as a hammer, screwdrivers and a tape measure.
fact: A toolbox can also mean a set of skills, methods or ideas you can use for a job.
fact: At school, a «toolbox» of strategies means number lines, drawing a picture and times tables for solving problems.
fact: In computing, a toolbox (or toolbar) holds the tools in a program.
fact: The words around a word, its context, show you which meaning is right.
exercise: Dad put the hammer and tape measure back in the «toolbox» in the shed. What is a toolbox here? | A bag for school books | A cupboard for food | A set of rules for a game | *A box for keeping and carrying tools
exercise: Ms Park says, «Use your maths toolbox: try a number line or draw a picture.» What does toolbox mean here? | A game about boxes | A box of metal tools | *A set of methods you can use to solve a problem | A list of things to buy from the shop
exercise: «Writers have a toolbox of hooks.» Which of these could be part of a writer's toolbox? | A tape measure | *Speech, action or a sound like «CRASH!» | A hammer and a screwdriver | A box of crayons
test: Which meaning of toolbox fits «Animals find the way with a whole toolbox»? | A nest in a tree | *A set of methods to find the way | A map printed on paper | A box of metal tools
test: A «calm-down toolbox» helps with feelings. What does toolbox mean here? | A loud alarm clock | A tin of plasters | A box of toys to throw away | *A set of ideas you can use to calm down
exam: In a computer program, what does the toolbox (or toolbar) hold? | *The tools of the program, shown in a row | A game with lots of boxes | A keyboard and a mouse | A box for putting away real tools
